{"archetypes":[{"name":"line-target-verifier","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan cites specific line numbers and case-arm names as insertion anchors; if any are stale the implementation lands in the wrong place or silently collides with an existing arm.","prompt_body":"Check every line-number claim and case-arm name cited in the plan against the actual content of `skills/review/scripts/test-aggregate-findings.sh`. Verify that the referenced arms (`zero_findings_nospace_pseudo_heading`, `zero_findings_prose_finding_ids`, `oos_shared_slot_merge`, `zero_findings_pure_attest`) exist at the stated positions and that the proposed new arm `zero_findings_nospace_pseudo_heading_with_attestation` does not already exist. Confirm the stub `case` block boundaries (~lines 81–363) and the insertion anchors (~line 221, ~line 920, ~lines 737–756) are accurate enough to produce a conflict-free sequential edit. Flag any claim where the stated line range or arm name diverges from the actual file content, since a misplaced insertion could silently skip both new tests. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"token-contract-verifier","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"New tests assert specific output tokens by value; if the production code emits different token strings the tests pass vacuously and never detect the targeted regressions.","prompt_body":"Verify that each output token asserted in the two new test blocks matches what `skills/review/scripts/aggregate-findings.sh` actually emits on the described code paths. Specifically check: (1) that `REASON=validation-exhausted` rather than `REASON=validation-failed` is the real emitted token on the `has_nonconforming_finding_heading_markers and has_attest_line` branch; (2) that `AGGREGATOR_VALIDATION_FAILED=nonconforming_heading_with_attestation` is the literal string written to the stderr file by the validator; (3) that `assert_whitespace_only` is defined in the test file and its semantics match the post-attest strip behavior described in the plan's edge-cases section. A mismatch between plan-asserted tokens and production-emitted tokens means both new tests will produce false passes regardless of code correctness. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
